        "id": "ch7_3_3-3",
        "text": "if not is_valid_transition(current_state, new_state):\nraise InvalidStateTransition(\"Invalid transition from\n{current_state} to {new_state}\")\ncheck_state_dependencies(new_state)\nvalidate_business_rules(new_state)\nHere\u2019s how this validation works in practice:\n1.\nTransition validation example:\nI Current state: \"on hold\" (for flight booking)\nI New state: \"confirmed\"\nI System checks the following:\nI Is payment received?\nI Are seats still available?\nI Is the price still valid?\n2.\nDependency checking example:\nI Booking includes flight and hotel\nI System verifies the following:\nI Hotel check-in time is after flight arrival\nI Transfer service availability matches flight time\nI Room type matches the number of travelers\n3.\nBusiness rules example:\nI International booking is being made\nI System ensures the following:\nI Passport information is provided\nI Travel insurance is offered\nI Cancellation policy is acknowledged\nAgent memory architecture and context management\n173\nIf any validation step fails, the system prevents the state change and raises an appropriate error,\nmaintaining the integrity of the booking system.",
